<div class="book-title">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim</div>
<div class="halacha-title">Hilchos Netilas Yadayim L'Seudah U'Betzi'as HaPas 3</div>
<div class="part-label">Part 2 — Sections 7–8</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 7  (continued from § 3 sub-sections)   -->
<!-- In the source these are labeled אות ג, ד, ה, ו -->
<!-- We continue where Part 1 ended                  -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

<div class="section-number">§ 3 (continued) — The Vessel and the <i>Medameh</i></div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, the vessel needs to be <span class="key-concept">complete</span>. For the water symbolizes the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> — the wondrous <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> that will be revealed in the future, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"And the earth will be full of the knowledge [<span class="heb-term">dei'ah</span>] of Hashem as the waters cover the sea"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Isaiah 11:9)</span>. And the primary <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> is to know Hashem — that is, to know and believe that He, blessed be He, is the Sole Primordial One; He is the Former, He is the Creator [who creates] something from absolute nothing — that is, the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world [<span class="heb-term">emunah d'chidush ha'olam</span>], as mentioned above, and as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. For through the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> — the aspect of <span class="verse">"and the earth will be full of knowledge"</span> etc. — one merits the levels mentioned above, until one merits this <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>: namely, the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, which is the main thing, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> mentioned above — which is the aspect of water — it is impossible to attain and receive except through a <span class="key-concept">vessel</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, which is in the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> <span class="heb-def">[the imaginative faculty]</span>, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. For the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is the vessel of the true <span class="heb-term">da'as</span>. For in truth, all the opinions of the entire world — even of the great philosophers and investigators — are all merely in the power of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>. For true <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> is only to know Hashem. And this, they have not even begun to attain or taste at all. For this <span class="heb-term">da'as</span>, no one merits except exceedingly great and awesome <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, singular individuals of the generations. But we — we do not have the power to attain this <span class="heb-term">da'as</span>. And we need to strengthen ourselves only with <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, which we merit through the refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> — which is refined through our meriting to draw close to true <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, these wicked <span class="heb-term">apikorsim</span> [heretics] — who do not want to rely on the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> of the holy <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, and who, in their loathsomeness and filth, immersed in all the desires, presume to investigate with their polluted intellect — therefore, in truth, their <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is intermingled and confused, until they come to great heresies or false beliefs. For it is impossible to draw and receive from the holy <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> except through meriting to sanctify and refine the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> through drawing close to true <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>. Through this, the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined. And then one merits complete holy <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>. For the primary <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> is in the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> — for in what the intellect comprehends, one does not need <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this refined <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> — it is the aspect of a <span class="key-concept">vessel that draws and receives the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span></span>. And this is hinted at in the Torah teaching mentioned above, where it is written at the end that all the titles and praises with which we describe Him, blessed be He, are all in the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, etc. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"on our festival day"</span> [<span class="heb-term">l'yom chagainu</span>], the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and with the compass he gives it form"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Isaiah 44:13)</span>, etc. — see there at the end. And this is the aspect of a vessel. For the plain meaning of the verse <span class="verse">"and with the compass he gives it form"</span> is said regarding the making of a vessel, as it is written there <span class="source-ref">(Isaiah 44)</span>: <span class="verse">"He shapes it with planes and with the compass he gives it form,"</span> etc.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And there, it speaks of the disgrace of false beliefs — of those who believe in idolatry, wood and stone, the works of human hands. And this is the aspect of vessels of the <span class="heb-term">sitra achra</span> — which are false beliefs, believing in wood and stone literally. But on the contrary, in holiness — the holy <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> in Hashem, blessed be He, which is in the aspect of the refined <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, through which one merits to describe and praise Him, blessed be He, with fitting titles and praises as is proper — all this is the aspect of a <span class="key-concept">vessel in the spiritual sense</span>. For the titles and praises with which we describe and praise Him are vessels to receive the perception of His G-dliness — each one according to what he estimates in his heart. For in truth, <span class="maxim">"no thought can grasp Him at all"</span>. Only through prayers and songs and praises — that is, titles and praises — which He, in His mercy, gave us permission to describe and praise Him with: through this, we have the power to draw upon ourselves the holy <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, through which vessels are made to receive the perception of His G-dliness — each one according to what he estimates in his heart.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, the vessel for <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> needs to be in completeness, without any blemish or deficiency — so that it can receive and contain the water, which is the aspect of the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> mentioned above, which is the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> that will be revealed in the future. And it is impossible to receive it except through a complete vessel — which is the aspect of the refined and rectified <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>. For when the vessel is broken and blemished, it is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"broken cisterns that cannot hold water"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Jeremiah 2:13)</span> — which is said regarding the idol-worshipping heretics who have false beliefs. Therefore, the vessel needs to be complete, in order to receive through it the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> mentioned above — through which one merits the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, as mentioned above. And through this, the primary subduing of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> [nourishment of the body] is accomplished, and one merits <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> [nourishment of the soul] — which is the primary intention of the washing, as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 4 (source: אות ד)                       -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 4 — Why Water Purifies from All Impurities</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And for this reason, <span class="key-concept">water purifies from all impurities</span>. And it is impossible to enter into any holiness without water — such as the <span class="heb-term">Kohanim</span> in their [Temple] service, and similarly in the morning upon rising, and similarly before prayer and Torah study, one needs to immerse or wash one's hands with water. And similarly, all the ritually impure do not ascend from their impurity except through water.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For water symbolizes the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> of the renewal of the world. For water preceded all of creation — for the beginning of creation was water, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said. It emerges that the primary renewal of the world began from water. And therefore, there is the primary root of the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> of the renewal of the world — through which the primary purification [is accomplished]. And only through this does one enter the service of Hashem. For this is the primary foundation of the holy <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> — to believe in the renewal of the world, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"In the beginning, G-d created the heavens"</span> etc. — which is the beginning of the Torah.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the primary holiness and purity. For conversely, all the impurities are drawn from the <span class="heb-term">zuhamas hanachash</span> [contamination of the serpent], which brought death — from which the primary impurity [comes]. And the primary [aspect] of the contamination of the serpent is the heresy of those who deny the renewal of the world, G-d forbid. And therefore, water — which is the aspect of the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> mentioned above, through which the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world is drawn — through this, [one achieves] all the purifications in the world. And it is impossible to enter any holiness or service except through water. For all holiness and all service of Hashem depend on this <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, which one merits to draw upon oneself through purification in water — through immersion or washing, according to the law. For through purification in water, one draws upon oneself the aspect of the illumination of the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> that will be revealed in the future — through which one merits the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, which is the foundation of the Torah and of service, as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 5 (source: אות ה) — Tisha B'Av         -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 5 — The Four Fasts and Tisha B'Av</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">four fasts</span> over the destruction of the <span class="heb-term">Bais HaMikdash</span> — which was caused by the sin of the spies, who wept on the night of <span class="heb-term">Tisha B'Av</span>, who blemished <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> — where the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world is revealed. And they blemished this. And through this, the <span class="heb-term">zuhamas hanachash</span> intensified, G-d forbid — <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, as mentioned above. Therefore one needs to fast, in order to subdue the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For when one merits complete <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, one does not need to fast. For through <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, the eating is in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> — which is the aspect of the eating of upright Jews, the aspect of eating on Shabbos. For through <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, the primary refinement of eating [is accomplished], as is explained elsewhere, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and graze on <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 37:3)</span>. But because they blemished <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> and blemished the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, as mentioned above — therefore, one needs to fast, to subdue the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> through the fast.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eichah</span> [Lamentations] that we recite on <span class="heb-term">Tisha B'Av</span>. And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"<span class="heb-term">Eichah</span> — how the gold has become dim"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:1)</span>. For the primary [subject of] the lamentations is over the <span class="key-concept">passing of the true <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span></span> — which is twice as [devastating as] the destruction of the <span class="heb-term">Bais HaMikdash</span>. And through this, we are now like <span class="verse">"sheep that have no shepherd."</span> For we do not know who the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span> is. And we need to cry out and search and seek: "<span class="heb-term">Eichah</span>! <span class="heb-term">Eichah</span>! [Where?! Where?!]" — [seeking] the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span> whose light has been darkened for us, for we do not merit to know of him. And this is: <span class="verse">"how the gold has become dim"</span> — the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, who is more precious than gold, has become dim, and his light has been darkened for us.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And it is not enough [that his light is hidden] — but our sorrow is compounded by more grief still. For <span class="verse">"the fine gold has changed"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:1)</span> — the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, who is likened to fine gold, has had his light so thoroughly darkened from Israel that the truth itself has been completely changed. For <span class="verse">"they call evil good and good evil"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Isaiah 5:20)</span>. And this is <span class="verse">"the fine gold has changed"</span> — that the fine gold, which is the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, has been changed. For they speak all manner of evil about him and change and exchange the truth for falsehood.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And through this: <span class="verse">"The holy stones are poured out at the head of every street"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:1)</span>. This is said regarding the hiddenness and concealment of the <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, who is the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">head of the house</span> [<span class="heb-term">rosh bayis</span>]. And the <span class="heb-term">mefursamim shel sheker</span> <span class="heb-def">[the falsely-famous ones]</span> intensify — who are the aspect of the <span class="verse">"head of every street"</span>, as is explained in the Torah teaching <span class="verse">"Beraishis–L'Einei"</span> etc. (see there, <span class="lm-ref">Likutay Moharan II, 67</span>).
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is: <span class="verse">"The precious children of Zion"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:2)</span>, etc. — as is explained there in the eulogy on <span class="heb-term">Parashas Eileh Toldos Noach</span>, see there in the above-mentioned <span class="heb-term">siman</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is: <span class="verse">"Even jackals offer the breast"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Lamentations 4:3)</span> etc. — which is the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">compassion of the <span class="heb-term">sitra achra</span></span> [false compassion], as is explained in the Torah teaching <span class="verse">"Tik'u-Tochachah"</span> mentioned above (<span class="lm-ref">Likutay Moharan II, 8</span>). For through this, the aspect of <span class="verse">"and the serpent was cunning"</span> intensifies, G-d forbid — through which all the troubles mentioned above are drawn, until one does not know about the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>. As is understood above: when one subdues the contamination of the serpent — which is the aspect of <span class="verse">"even jackals offer the breast"</span>, etc. — through the prayer of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span> [the man of power], then one merits all the levels mentioned above, until the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined through the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>, as mentioned above. And the reverse, the reverse, G-d forbid [when the serpent intensifies]. And then one does not know: <span class="heb-term">Eichah</span>! Where is the light of the true <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>? And over this we lament: <span class="verse">"<span class="heb-term">Eichah</span> — how the gold has become dim"</span> — which is said regarding the passing and concealment of the light of the <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  But through the lamentations and the crying "<span class="heb-term">Eichah</span>!" — we merit that his light should be revealed to us, and we merit complete <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, until the song of the future is aroused — and then the joy will be very great. And as our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="maxim">"Rejoice with her, rejoice — all who mourn over her"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Ta'anis 30b)</span>, etc.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of <span class="key-concept"><span class="heb-term">Shabbos Chazon</span></span>. <span class="heb-term">Chazon</span> [Vision] specifically — meaning, prophecy. For the primary rectification that we need now is to return and draw down the emanation of prophecy — through which the primary refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> [is accomplished], through which the completeness of <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> [comes], as mentioned above. For on Shabbos is the primary rectification. For <span class="maxim">"Shabbos protected him"</span> — it protected Adam HaRishon, who blemished all the above. And <span class="maxim">"Shabbos protected him."</span> And therefore, this Shabbos before <span class="heb-term">Tisha B'Av</span> is called <span class="heb-term">Shabbos Chazon</span> — to indicate that we need now, on this Shabbos, to rectify the aspect of <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, whose primary [source] depends on prophecy, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. And therefore it is called <span class="heb-term">Shabbos Chazon</span> — in the language of prophecy, as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 6 (source: אות ו) — Names of Tzadikim  -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 6 — The Names of the <i>Tzadikim</i></div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of what <span class="heb-term">Rabbainu</span>, of blessed memory, wrote in <span class="heb-term">Sefer HaAlef-Bais HeChadash</span>, entry <span class="heb-term">Tzadik</span>, §20 — that through the <span class="key-concept">mentioning of the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span></span>, one can bring about renewal in the work of Creation — that is, to change nature. For it is explained in the Torah teaching <span class="verse">"Tik'u-Tochachah"</span> mentioned above that every <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span> has the aspect of a spirit of prophecy, <span class="heb-term">ru'ach hakodesh</span> [the Holy Spirit] — through which the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> of all those who draw close to him is refined. And through this, one merits the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world. And through this <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, there will be the renewal of the world in the future — when the world will be conducted in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, meaning in the aspect of Providence and wonders, not in the way of nature — see there, all this is explained well.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, through mentioning the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> — through this, the <span class="heb-term">reshimu</span> <span class="heb-def">[residual imprint]</span> of them is aroused, as <span class="heb-term">Rabbainu</span>, of blessed memory, wrote elsewhere (<span class="lm-ref">Likutay Moharan I, 248</span>) — that through telling stories of <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, their <span class="heb-term">reshimu</span> is aroused. And therefore, through the mentioning of their names, the power of their <span class="heb-term">reshimu</span> and of their good deeds is aroused. And the primary power of the good deeds of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> is that through their good deeds, they merited the aspect of <span class="heb-term">ru'ach hakodesh</span>. And they drew down through this the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, through the mentioning of their names, one can certainly bring about change in the work of Creation — that is, to change nature. For through the mentioning of the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, the power of their <span class="heb-term">ru'ach hakodesh</span> is aroused, and the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world is drawn into the world. And through this, an illumination is drawn from the renewal of the world in the future — which will come about through this, as mentioned above. For then, the world will be conducted in the aspect of Providence and wonders, not in the way of nature. And therefore, one can certainly change nature through this.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is what <span class="heb-term">Rabbainu</span>, of blessed memory, wrote — that one should write down for himself the <span class="key-concept">names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> as a remembrance</span> (as it is written in the <span class="heb-term">Alef-Bais HaYashan</span>, entry <span class="heb-term">Tzadik</span>, §19): "One for whom Hashem, blessed be He, is precious in his eyes — let him write for himself in a book the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> and the <span class="heb-term">Tanna'im</span> and the G-d-fearing ones, as a remembrance."
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For one needs to write their names as a remembrance. For the primary power of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> — who reveal the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, as mentioned above — is through their refining the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, through the aspect of <span class="heb-term">ru'ach hakodesh</span>, the spirit of prophecy that is theirs, as is explained there in the Torah teaching mentioned above. For the primary <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> is through the refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, one needs to write their names in a book specifically. For writing is for the sake of remembrance, as it is written: <span class="verse">"Write this as a remembrance in a book"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Exodus 17:14)</span>. And <span class="key-concept">remembrance is in the power of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span></span>, as <span class="heb-term">Rabbainu</span>, of blessed memory, wrote elsewhere. And the name is the aspect of remembrance, as it is written: <span class="verse">"Your Name and Your remembrance are the desire of the soul"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Isaiah 26:8)</span>. And as it is written: <span class="verse">"This is My Name forever, and this is My remembrance for all generations"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Exodus 3:15)</span>. And it is written: <span class="verse">"Hashem, Your Name is forever; Hashem, Your remembrance is for all generations"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 135:13)</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  Therefore, through the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> — which are the aspect of remembrance, the aspect of: <span class="maxim">"the remembrance of a <span class="heb-term">tzadik</span> is for a blessing"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Proverbs 10:7)</span> — for the primary remembrance that remains of all the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> is their holy name, that their remembrance remains in the world as a blessing — therefore, through the mentioning of their holy names, in which His Name, blessed be He, is partnered with their names — through this, the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined. For their holy name, which is the aspect of remembrance — which is in the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> — therefore, the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined through the remembrance of the holy names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, whose entire service was to refine the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, etc., as mentioned above. And therefore, the mentioning of their names is especially <span class="heb-term">mesugal</span> <span class="heb-def">[auspicious / efficacious]</span> for this — for their names themselves are the aspect of the refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>. For their name is the aspect of the rectification of remembrance, which is the rectification of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, where remembrance resides, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, one needs to write their names in a book specifically. For writing is for remembrance, the aspect of <span class="verse">"write this as a remembrance in a book."</span> And through this, the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined, as mentioned above. And therefore, all the words of the Prophets need to be written in a book. For all the twenty-four books of the Prophets are the aspect of the Written Torah, which it is forbidden to recite orally. For prophecy is the refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, as mentioned above. Therefore, they need to be written specifically. For writing is the aspect of remembrance, which is the aspect of the refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, as mentioned above. And this is the aspect of writing the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> as a remembrance. For all of this is the aspect of the refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> — which is refined through the merit and power of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, as mentioned above. And through this, one merits the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world — through which one changes nature, as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 7 (source: אות ז) — Pinchas             -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 7 — Pinchas and the Names of the Families</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And all of this is merited through the prayer in the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">judgment of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span></span> [the man of power], as is explained well in the Torah teaching mentioned above — that through the prayer of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span>, one merits to make converts and to increase His glory, blessed be He, and to draw down prophecy — through which the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined. It emerges that the power of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> who refine the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is drawn from the prayer of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span> mentioned above — through which one merits the spirit of prophecy — through which the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is why <span class="key-concept"><span class="heb-term">Parashas</span> <span class="verse">"Se'u es rosh Bnei Yisrael"</span></span> <span class="source-ref">(Numbers 26:2)</span> is juxtaposed with <span class="heb-term">Parashas Pinchas ben Elazar</span>, etc. For Pinchas turned back the wrath of Hashem, blessed be He, and sweetened the judgment from Israel through prayer in the aspect of judgment, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"And Pinchas stood and prayed, and the plague was stayed"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 106:30)</span>, as is explained well at the beginning of the Torah teaching mentioned above — see there. And therefore, immediately after this — after the verse mentions the great power of Pinchas, who turned back His wrath, etc. (all of which was through his prayer in the aspect of judgment, as mentioned above, through which all the levels mentioned above are accomplished — from which the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> receive the spirit of prophecy, through which the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined, and one merits <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> and the renewal of the world of the future, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>; and for this reason, the mentioning of the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> is especially auspicious, as mentioned above) —
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  — and this is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Parashas</span> <span class="verse">"Se'u es rosh Bnei Yisrael l'mishpechosam"</span> — where the <span class="key-concept">names of all the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span></span> are mentioned, who are the heads of the families of the children of Israel — in which Hashem, blessed be He, partnered His Name with their names. As it is written: <span class="verse">"HaChanochi, HaPalui"</span> — as Rashi explains: "My Name testifies upon them." It emerges that all the names of the families mentioned there in <span class="heb-term">Parashas Pinchas</span> are all the aspect of the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, in which His Name, blessed be He, is partnered. And therefore, how good and beautiful is the juxtaposition of this <span class="heb-term">parsha</span> to the matter of Pinchas ben Elazar — who is the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span> who prayed the prayer in the aspect of judgment, from which the power of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> is drawn, etc. And for this reason, the mentioning of their names is especially auspicious, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And now, how beautiful and fitting that immediately after this is juxtaposed the <span class="key-concept"><span class="heb-term">parsha</span> of the inheritance of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span></span>, as it is written there: <span class="verse">"To these the land shall be divided as an inheritance, by the number of names; to the names of the tribes of their fathers they shall inherit"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Numbers 26:53, 55)</span>. For all the levels mentioned above are the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>. For the renewal of the world in the future — which is merited through all the above — is in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, as mentioned above. Understand this well. And this is: <span class="verse">"to these the land shall be divided as an inheritance, <b>by the number of names</b>"</span> — "by the number of names" specifically; <span class="verse">"<b>to the names</b> of the tribes of their fathers"</span> — specifically. Meaning, the aspect of the names of the <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> — through which the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is refined and one merits <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> — and through this, one merits the renewal of the world of the future, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, as mentioned above. Understand this well.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 8 (source: אות ח)                       -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 8 — Why <i>Netilas Yadayim</i> Only for the Five Species of Grain</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, one is only obligated in <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> for bread over which one recites <span class="heb-term">HaMotzi</span> and <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span>. And <span class="heb-term">HaMotzi</span> and <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span> are only recited upon the <span class="key-concept">five species with which <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> was praised</span>. For the primary mitzvah of <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span> is only to bless Him, blessed be He, for having given us <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> — as it is written: <span class="verse">"And you shall eat and be satisfied, and you shall bless Hashem your G-d <b>for the good land</b>"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Deuteronomy 8:10)</span>, etc.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For the primary holiness of eating is through <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> — which is the aspect of the renewal of the world of the future, through which the song of the future is drawn — through which one merits that the eating should be in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above. And for this reason, the primary mitzvah of <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> is for this purpose, as mentioned above. And therefore, the primary <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> is over the five species specifically, which are obligated in <span class="heb-term">Birchas HaMazon</span>, which are the praise of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>. For the primary [purpose of] <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> is to draw the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> through the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> — in order to merit the song mentioned above, so that the eating should be in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph" style="text-align: center; font-style: italic; color: var(--accent-muted); margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  And there is still much more to say about this. Hashem, blessed be He, should grant us to draw complete <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> into the world, and may we return to <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> speedily in our days. And may there be fulfilled: <span class="verse">"You shall come, you shall gaze, from the peak of <span class="heb-term">Amanah</span>"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Song of Songs 4:8)</span> — speedily in our days, Amen.
</div>

<!-- Translator's Summary -->
<div class="translator-summary">
  <div class="summary-heading">✦ Translator's Summary — Part 2 ✦</div>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    This concluding portion of Halacha 3 expands into some of the broadest themes in Breslov thought:
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>The <em>medameh</em> (imaginative faculty):</strong> The key vessel. All human "knowledge" — even that of the greatest philosophers — is merely the <em>medameh</em>. True <em>da'as</em> (knowing Hashem) is attained only by the <em>tzadikim</em>. For us, the path is through refining the <em>medameh</em> by drawing close to true <em>tzadikim</em>, which gives us <em>emunah</em>. A broken <em>medameh</em> = "broken cisterns that cannot hold water" = false beliefs; a refined <em>medameh</em> = a complete vessel that can receive the waters of <em>da'as</em>.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>Water and Creation:</strong> Water preceded all creation — therefore it contains the root of the <em>da'as</em> of the renewal of the world. All purification (mikveh, hand-washing, the Kohanim's service) works through water because it draws down the <em>emunah</em> of <em>chidush ha'olam</em>.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>Tisha B'Av:</strong> The lamentations are primarily over the <em>concealment of the true tzadik</em>. "<em>Eichah</em> — how the gold has become dim" = Where is the light of the <em>tzadik</em>? Even worse: "the fine gold has <em>changed</em>" — the truth is inverted, "they call evil good and good evil." But through the crying of <em>Eichah</em> itself, the light is restored.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>Names of the <em>Tzadikim</em>:</strong> Mentioning their names arouses their <em>reshimu</em> (spiritual imprint), which refines the <em>medameh</em> and draws <em>emunah</em> of <em>chidush ha'olam</em>. This is why <em>Parashas Pinchas</em> lists the family names (with Hashem's Name partnered in them) and immediately follows with the inheritance of <em>Eretz Yisrael</em>.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>The closing prayer:</strong> "May we return to <em>Eretz Yisrael</em> speedily… from the peak of <em>Amanah</em> [<em>emunah</em>]."
  </p>
</div>


